phase P4
title Persistence and evidence
tasks
    T400
        title        Implement persistence providers and storage adapters
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V1,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.1 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-004, PROOF-009, PROOF-014, HOST-P04.

            Deliver an inert Runtime-owned persistence provider, storage read/write/
            remove, Web Storage and IndexedDB adapters, pure synchronous codecs,
            identity-only filters, per-family persistence declarations, and ordered,
            coalesced writes with truthful final flush.

            Absorb the provider, storage, codec, and persistence-lifetime proof
            obligations from retired flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed). Cross-file blocker:
            P3 task T306, in workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete before
            implementation. Coordinate with the Rewrite integrator. Keep the private
            persistence owner and local tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/persistence/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns providers, storage adapters,
            and provider lifecycle. Keep public exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Construction and an absent provider perform no storage I/O.
            - Writes remain ordered; failures preserve Runtime truth and the last good
            record. Filters cannot mutate data or select undeclared records.
            - Web Storage and IndexedDB failures retain typed categories. Default and
            custom codecs reject malformed data; custom-codec failure changes no
            Runtime state and retains the last good record.
            - Focused provider tests and nub run lint pass for the changed slice.

    T401
        title        Implement durable identity and boot restoration
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T400, @task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V2,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.2 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-002, PROOF-004, PROOF-009, PROOF-014, HOST-P01, HOST-P04.

            Deliver the private immutable boot carrier, exact app and persistence
            identity, module/machine resolution, stable-ref encoding and bindings.
            Order the boot stages as pure detached preparation, then Implementation
            acquisition, then actor/Store installation, graph sealing, and activation.

            Absorb the durable-reference and boot-identity proof obligations from
            retired flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed). Cross-file blocker: P3 task T306, in
            workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete before implementation.
            Keep the private boot-restoration owner and local tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/persistence/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns identity validation and
            provider-first restoration during actor/Store installation. Keep public
            exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Foreign, malformed, duplicate, or ambiguous identity fails before
            activation; opaque references cannot restore.
            - Prepare and validate the boot carrier while detached, without actor or
            Store installation. Acquire Implementation only after preparation; then
            install the baseline silently, restoring providers before consumers, seal
            the graph, and activate. Do not replay input, initializers, or streamed
            outcomes. Opaque providers fail closed.
            Mismatched app data cannot cross Runtimes.
            - Stable-reference vectors cover UTF-8 boundaries, composed spelling,
            decomposed spelling, and lone-surrogate rejection on pinned Node.
            - Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit pass the compact same-codec
            portability fixture. Focused tests and nub run lint pass.

    T402
        title        Implement context-closed capture and hydration
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T400, @T401, @task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V2,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Artifacts.O3]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.3 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-004, PROOF-009, PROOF-013, PROOF-014, HOST-P04, SNAP-P01.

            Deliver one capture barrier shared with Store commits, stable actor and
            provider closure, one consistent Store revision, declaration filtering,
            and normalization of restored resources, interrupted or unknown
            transactions, and new-generation streams. Fence stale writes and flush on
            disposal.

            Absorb capture, hydration, and persistence/evidence-boundary proof
            obligations from retired flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed). Cross-file blocker:
            P3 task T306, in workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete first.
            Keep the private capture and hydration owner and local tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/persistence/ and its local test/ subtree.
            Within this owner directory, this task owns consistent capture and
            restoration normalization. Keep public exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Concurrent capture returns the specified retryable failure; no capture
            observes a half-published Store state.
            - Local, opaque, disposed, or tombstoned actors are excluded. Live cells,
            fibers, scopes, cursors, commands, and emissions are never persisted.
            - Missing stream input and non-durable context fail closed. Hydration does
            not replay input or events, restores context in dependency order, and
            stale writes cannot replace newer truth. Concurrent capture remains
            retryable and custom-codec failure commits no Runtime mutation.
            - Focused capture and hydration tests and nub run lint pass.

    T403
        title        Implement the canonical bounded wire model
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T401, @T402, @task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V5,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Artifacts.O4]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.4 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-010, PROOF-014, REV-MIG-005.

            Deliver one package-private decoded model, canonical strict UTF-8 parser
            and encoder, exact behavior/trace/diagnostic/Story failure/checkpoint/
            record/operation/CLI unions, AppPlan fingerprint, canonical ordering,
            bounded identity and envelope, and at most one gzip member.

            Absorb canonical wire, fingerprint, bounds, and parser proof obligations
            from retired flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed). Cross-file blocker: Phase 3
            P3 task T306, in workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete first. Keep
            wire ownership in the private codec module under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/wire/ and its existing tests/ subtree.
            Keep public exports on their existing routes.
        acceptance
            - Public-byte round trips and negative vectors enforce strict UTF-8,
            canonical ordering, exact bounds, fingerprints, and legacy rejection.
            - Detectable duplicate keys, malformed unions, required nulls, trailing
            bytes, and multiple gzip members fail with stable diagnostics.
            - Invalid identities, ownership, defaults, Story metadata, lifecycle
            tuples, and inconsistent trace evidence reject before activation with
            typed diagnostics.
            - Full vectors pass on pinned Node; Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit
            pass the compact shared-codec fixture.
            - Tests exercise public byte paths, not private hostile reflection input.
            Focused codec tests and nub run lint pass.

    T404
        title        Implement inspection evidence and share artifacts
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T403, @task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.D2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C4,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V4,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V5,
                     @plan.Verification.V6,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V6
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.5 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-010, PROOF-013, PROOF-014, API-P04.

            Deliver one-attachment asynchronous inspection sinks, exact snapshot and
            clear surface, caller capacity and default, globally ordered accepted
            evidence, accepted-prefix drain, pure inspection, defensive raw artifact
            bytes, fixed-path share redaction, canonical tuple manifests, and immutable
            Story evidence/failure projections.

            Absorb artifact, sink, Story-evidence, and inspection proof obligations
            from retired flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed). Provenance: flow-state-e7p.4.8
            (closed decision) and flow-state-e7p.4.9 (closed contract reconciliation)
            define the share export input; neither adds a separate implementation.
            The share encoder belongs in the single private artifact module under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/wire/; inspection sink ownership stays
            under packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/evidence/. Keep tests in
            those modules' test/ or existing tests/ subtrees. Cross-file blocker: P3
            task T306, in workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete. Coordinate
            CLI-facing coverage with the Phase 5 integrator.
        acceptance
            - Sinks cannot block or mutate Runtime truth and detach on failure.
            Capacity zero, default capacity, late attachment, clear, drain, and
            disposal have observable production-owner proofs.
            - Evidence ordering and truncation are exact; Story evidence is immutable,
            and raw Cause is not serialized.
            - Share output mirrors the complete raw trace under its distinct identity,
            preserves identity and order, and redacts only listed paths. Each listed
            path resolves to the fixed replacement in canonical tuple order; raw
            Runtime truth, persistence, and evidence remain unchanged. Raw import
            rejects share data as WrongArtifactKind.
            - Missing, duplicate, overlapping, or structural redaction paths reject;
            no new public export route is implied by these private owner locations.
            - Empty share policy returns byte-identical raw output. No CLI, replay,
            persistence, boot, or evidence-authority share input is added.
            - Focused evidence and artifact tests and nub run lint pass.

    T405
        title        Validate Phase 4 owners and proof coverage
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T400, @T401, @T402, @T403, @T404, @task.Rewrite.T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.D2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C4,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V4,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V5,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.4.7 (open); phase Bead:
            flow-state-e7p.4 (open).

            Run the read-only Phase 4 correctness gate over changed slices and named
            production-owner proofs. Review only Phase 4 changes, direct trace
            provenance, feature layout, failure and cleanup lanes, and required
            retention/deletion evidence. Do not re-audit unchanged phases or the full
            contract pack.

            The retired proof tracker flow-state-e7p.4.6 (closed) is absorbed by
            T400–T404; its closure did not claim completed proofs. Cross-file blocker:
            P3 task T306, in workflow/tasks/Rewrite/P3.task, must complete first.
            Coordinate the remaining CLI-facing proof with the Phase 5 integrator.

            Outcome disposition: T402 owns Artifacts O3 and T403 owns O4. O1 spans
            T400 and T402; O2 spans T401 and T402; O5 spans P3 T305 and T404; O6
            spans T403 and T404. These outcomes remain deferred until those owners
            deliver the integrated behavior and proof coverage. O7 remains with the
            Story/model task in Phase 5.
        acceptance
            - Every named Phase 4 invariant has a decisive production-path proof;
            focused checks and nub run lint pass for changed slices.
            - Check Verification V6 across restore-before-activation, context closure,
            persistence failures, bounded artifact validation, sink ordering, and
            redaction. Confirm no replay, partial restore, or share import path remains.
            - Return Contract IDs; Changed files; Focused checks; Lint pass/fail;
            Behavior reviewed; Fixed findings; Blocking findings; Remaining advisory
            findings.
            - No blocking finding, unclassified proof gap, hidden compatibility,
            duplicate authority, cast/any erasure, uncontrolled async work, partial
            update, or implementation-detail-only proof remains.
            - Equivalent durable UTF-8 and stable-reference vectors pass on pinned
            Node, Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit. No compile-time UTF-8
            tables are required.
